# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Yaml Front Matter Hash Value: title
#, no-wrap
msgid "Multiple systems and reduced states"
msgstr "Vícenásobné systémy a redukované stavy"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "{/* cspell:ignore operatorname */}\n"
msgstr "{/* cspell:ignore operatorname */}\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Now we'll turn our attention to how density matrices work for multiple "
"systems, including examples of different types of correlations they can "
"express and how they can be used to describe the states of isolated parts of"
" compound systems.\n"
msgstr ""
"Nyní se zaměříme na to, jak matice hustoty fungují pro více systémů, včetně "
"příkladů různých typů korelací, které mohou vyjádřit, a jak je lze použít k "
"popisu stavů izolovaných částí složených systémů.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Title ##
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Multiple systems {#multiple-systems}"
msgstr "Vice systémů {#multiple-systems}"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Density matrices can represent states of multiple systems in an analogous way to state vectors in the simplified formulation of quantum information, following the same basic idea that multiple systems can be viewed as if they're single, compound systems.\n"
"In mathematical terms, the rows and columns of density matrices representing states of multiple systems are placed in correspondence with the Cartesian product of the classical state sets of the individual systems.\n"
msgstr ""
"Matice hustoty mohou reprezentovat stavy více systémů analogickým způsobem jako stavové vektory ve zjednodušené formulaci kvantové informace, přičemž se řídí stejnou základní myšlenkou, že více systémů lze nahlížet, jako by tvořily jeden složený systém.\n"
"Matematicky řečeno, řádky a sloupce matic hustoty reprezentujících stavy více systémů odpovídají kartézskému součinu množin klasických stavů jednotlivých systémů.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"For example, recall the state vector representations of the four Bell "
"states.\n"
msgstr ""
"Připomeň si například reprezentace čtyř Bellových stavů pomocí stavových "
"vektorů.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{aligned}\n"
"  \\vert \\phi^+ \\rangle & = \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}} \\vert 00 \\rangle + \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}} \\vert 11 \\rangle \\\\[2mm]\n"
"  \\vert \\phi^- \\rangle & = \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}} \\vert 00 \\rangle - \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}} \\vert 11 \\rangle \\\\[2mm]\n"
"  \\vert \\psi^+ \\rangle & = \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}} \\vert 01 \\rangle + \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}} \\vert 10 \\rangle \\\\[2mm]\n"
"  \\vert \\psi^- \\rangle & = \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}} \\vert 01 \\rangle - \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}} \\vert 10 \\rangle\n"
"\\end{aligned}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{aligned}\n"
"  \\vert \\phi^+ \\rangle & = \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}} \\vert 00 \\rangle + \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}} \\vert 11 \\rangle \\\\[2mm]\n"
"  \\vert \\phi^- \\rangle & = \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}} \\vert 00 \\rangle - \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}} \\vert 11 \\rangle \\\\[2mm]\n"
"  \\vert \\psi^+ \\rangle & = \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}} \\vert 01 \\rangle + \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}} \\vert 10 \\rangle \\\\[2mm]\n"
"  \\vert \\psi^- \\rangle & = \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}} \\vert 01 \\rangle - \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}} \\vert 10 \\rangle\n"
"\\end{aligned}\n"
"$$\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "The density matrix representations of these states are as follows.\n"
msgstr "Reprezentace těchto stavů pomocí matic hustoty jsou následující.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\vert \\phi^+ \\rangle \\langle \\phi^+ \\vert =\n"
"\\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"  \\frac{1}{2} & 0 & 0 & \\frac{1}{2}\\\\[2mm]\n"
"  0 & 0 & 0 & 0\\\\[2mm]\n"
"  0 & 0 & 0 & 0\\\\[2mm]\n"
"  \\frac{1}{2} & 0 & 0 & \\frac{1}{2}\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\vert \\phi^+ \\rangle \\langle \\phi^+ \\vert =\n"
"\\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"  \\frac{1}{2} & 0 & 0 & \\frac{1}{2}\\\\[2mm]\n"
"  0 & 0 & 0 & 0\\\\[2mm]\n"
"  0 & 0 & 0 & 0\\\\[2mm]\n"
"  \\frac{1}{2} & 0 & 0 & \\frac{1}{2}\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\n"
"$$\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\vert \\phi^- \\rangle \\langle \\phi^- \\vert =\n"
"\\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"  \\frac{1}{2} & 0 & 0 & -\\frac{1}{2}\\\\[2mm]\n"
"  0 & 0 & 0 & 0\\\\[2mm]\n"
"  0 & 0 & 0 & 0\\\\[2mm]\n"
"  -\\frac{1}{2} & 0 & 0 & \\frac{1}{2}\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\vert \\phi^- \\rangle \\langle \\phi^- \\vert =\n"
"\\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"  \\frac{1}{2} & 0 & 0 & -\\frac{1}{2}\\\\[2mm]\n"
"  0 & 0 & 0 & 0\\\\[2mm]\n"
"  0 & 0 & 0 & 0\\\\[2mm]\n"
"  -\\frac{1}{2} & 0 & 0 & \\frac{1}{2}\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\n"
"$$\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\vert \\psi^+ \\rangle \\langle \\psi^+ \\vert =\n"
"\\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"  0 & 0 & 0 & 0\\\\[2mm]\n"
"  0 & \\frac{1}{2} & \\frac{1}{2} & 0\\\\[2mm]\n"
"  0 & \\frac{1}{2} & \\frac{1}{2} & 0\\\\[2mm]\n"
"  0 & 0 & 0 & 0\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\vert \\psi^+ \\rangle \\langle \\psi^+ \\vert =\n"
"\\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"  0 & 0 & 0 & 0\\\\[2mm]\n"
"  0 & \\frac{1}{2} & \\frac{1}{2} & 0\\\\[2mm]\n"
"  0 & \\frac{1}{2} & \\frac{1}{2} & 0\\\\[2mm]\n"
"  0 & 0 & 0 & 0\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\n"
"$$\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\vert \\psi^- \\rangle \\langle \\psi^- \\vert =\n"
"\\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"  0 & 0 & 0 & 0\\\\[2mm]\n"
"  0 & \\frac{1}{2} & -\\frac{1}{2} & 0\\\\[2mm]\n"
"  0 & -\\frac{1}{2} & \\frac{1}{2} & 0\\\\[2mm]\n"
"  0 & 0 & 0 & 0\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\vert \\psi^- \\rangle \\langle \\psi^- \\vert =\n"
"\\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"  0 & 0 & 0 & 0\\\\[2mm]\n"
"  0 & \\frac{1}{2} & -\\frac{1}{2} & 0\\\\[2mm]\n"
"  0 & -\\frac{1}{2} & \\frac{1}{2} & 0\\\\[2mm]\n"
"  0 & 0 & 0 & 0\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\n"
"$$\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Title ###
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Product states {#product-states}"
msgstr "Produktové stavy {#product-states}"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Similar to what we had for state vectors, tensor products of density matrices represent *independence* between the states of multiple systems.\n"
"For instance, if $\\mathsf{X}$ is prepared in the state represented by the density matrix $\\rho$ and $\\mathsf{Y}$ is independently prepared in the state represented by $\\sigma,$ then the density matrix describing the state of $(\\mathsf{X},\\mathsf{Y})$ is the tensor product $\\rho\\otimes\\sigma.$\n"
msgstr ""
"Podobně jako u stavových vektorů, tenzorové součiny matic hustoty reprezentují *nezávislost* mezi stavy více systémů.\n"
"Například pokud je $\\mathsf{X}$ připraven ve stavu reprezentovaném maticí hustoty $\\rho$ a $\\mathsf{Y}$ je nezávisle připraven ve stavu reprezentovaném $\\sigma,$ pak matice hustoty popisující stav $(\\mathsf{X},\\mathsf{Y})$ je tenzorový součin $\\rho\\otimes\\sigma.$\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The same terminology is used here as in the simplified formulation of "
"quantum information: states of this form are referred to as *product "
"states*.\n"
msgstr ""
"Používá se zde stejná terminologie jako ve zjednodušené formulaci kvantové "
"informace: stavy tohoto tvaru se nazývají *produktové stavy*.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Title ###
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Correlated and entangled states {#correlated-and-entangled-states}"
msgstr "Korelované a provázané stavy {#correlated-and-entangled-states}"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"States that cannot be expressed as product states represent *correlations* between systems.\n"
"There are, in fact, different types of correlations that can be represented by density matrices.\n"
"Here are a few examples.\n"
msgstr ""
"Stavy, které nelze vyjádřit jako produktové stavy, reprezentují *korelace* mezi systémy.\n"
"Ve skutečnosti existují různé typy korelací, které lze maticemi hustoty reprezentovat.\n"
"Zde je několik příkladů.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Bullet: '1. '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"*Correlated classical states.*\n"
"For example, we can express the situation in which Alice and Bob share a random bit like this:\n"
msgstr ""
"*Korelované klasické stavy.*\n"
"Například situaci, kdy Alice a Bob sdílejí náhodný bit, můžeme vyjádřit takto:\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"   $$\n"
"   \\frac{1}{2} \\vert 0 \\rangle \\langle 0 \\vert \\otimes \\vert 0 \\rangle \\langle 0 \\vert +\n"
"   \\frac{1}{2} \\vert 1 \\rangle \\langle 1 \\vert \\otimes \\vert 1 \\rangle \\langle 1 \\vert\n"
"   =\n"
"   \\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"   \\frac{1}{2} & 0 & 0 & 0\\\\[2mm]\n"
"   0 & 0 & 0 & 0\\\\[2mm]\n"
"   0 & 0 & 0 & 0\\\\[2mm]\n"
"   0 & 0 & 0 & \\frac{1}{2}\n"
"   \\end{pmatrix}\n"
"   $$\n"
msgstr ""
"   $$\n"
"   \\frac{1}{2} \\vert 0 \\rangle \\langle 0 \\vert \\otimes \\vert 0 \\rangle \\langle 0 \\vert +\n"
"   \\frac{1}{2} \\vert 1 \\rangle \\langle 1 \\vert \\otimes \\vert 1 \\rangle \\langle 1 \\vert\n"
"   =\n"
"   \\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"   \\frac{1}{2} & 0 & 0 & 0\\\\[2mm]\n"
"   0 & 0 & 0 & 0\\\\[2mm]\n"
"   0 & 0 & 0 & 0\\\\[2mm]\n"
"   0 & 0 & 0 & \\frac{1}{2}\n"
"   \\end{pmatrix}\n"
"   $$\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Bullet: '2. '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"*Ensembles of quantum states.*\n"
"Suppose we have $m$ density matrices $\\rho_0,\\ldots,\\rho_{m-1},$ all representing states of a system $\\mathsf{X},$ and we  randomly choose one of these states according to a probability vector $(p_0,\\ldots,p_{m-1}).$ Such a process is represented by an *ensemble* of states, which includes the specification of the density matrices $\\rho_0,\\ldots,\\rho_{m-1},$ as well as the probabilities $(p_0,\\ldots,p_{m-1}).$ We can associate an ensemble of states with a single density matrix, describing both the random choice of $k$ and the corresponding density matrix $\\rho_k,$ like this:\n"
msgstr ""
"*Soubory kvantových stavů.*\n"
"Předpokládejme, že máme $m$ matic hustoty $\\rho_0,\\ldots,\\rho_{m-1},$ všechny reprezentující stavy systému $\\mathsf{X},$ a náhodně vybereme jeden z těchto stavů podle vektoru pravděpodobnosti $(p_0,\\ldots,p_{m-1}).$ Takový proces je reprezentován *souborem* (ensemble) stavů, který zahrnuje specifikaci matic hustoty $\\rho_0,\\ldots,\\rho_{m-1},$ stejně jako pravděpodobnosti $(p_0,\\ldots,p_{m-1}).$ Souboru stavů můžeme přiřadit jedinou matici hustoty, popisující jak náhodný výběr $k,$ tak odpovídající matici hustoty $\\rho_k,$ a to takto:\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"   $$\n"
"   \\sum_{k = 0}^{m-1} p_k \\vert k\\rangle \\langle k \\vert \\otimes \\rho_k.\n"
"   $$\n"
msgstr ""
"   $$\n"
"   \\sum_{k = 0}^{m-1} p_k \\vert k\\rangle \\langle k \\vert \\otimes \\rho_k.\n"
"   $$\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"   To be clear, this is the state of a pair $(\\mathsf{Y},\\mathsf{X})$ "
"where $\\mathsf{Y}$ represents the classical selection of $k$ — so we're "
"assuming its classical state set is $\\{0,\\ldots,m-1\\}.$ States of this "
"form are sometimes called *classical-quantum states*.\n"
msgstr ""
"   Pro upřesnění, toto je stav dvojice $(\\mathsf{Y},\\mathsf{X}),$ kde "
"$\\mathsf{Y}$ reprezentuje klasický výběr $k$ — takže předpokládáme, že jeho"
" množina klasických stavů je $\\{0,\\ldots,m-1\\}.$ Stavy tohoto tvaru se "
"někdy nazývají *klasicko-kvantové stavy*.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Bullet: '3. '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"*Separable states*. We can imagine situations in which we have a classical "
"correlation among the quantum states of two systems like this:\n"
msgstr ""
"*Separabilní stavy*. Můžeme si představit situace, ve kterých máme klasickou"
" korelaci mezi kvantovými stavy dvou systémů, a to takto:\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"   $$\n"
"   \\sum_{k = 0}^{m-1} p_k \\rho_k \\otimes \\sigma_k.\n"
"   $$\n"
msgstr ""
"   $$\n"
"   \\sum_{k = 0}^{m-1} p_k \\rho_k \\otimes \\sigma_k.\n"
"   $$\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"   In words, for each $k$ from $0$ to $m-1,$ we have that with probability "
"$p_k$ the system on the left is in the state $\\rho_k$ and the system on the"
" right is in the state $\\sigma_k.$ States like this are called *separable "
"states*. This concept can also be extended to more than two systems.\n"
msgstr ""
"   Slovy řečeno, pro každé $k$ od $0$ do $m-1$ platí, že s pravděpodobností "
"$p_k$ je systém vlevo ve stavu $\\rho_k$ a systém vpravo ve stavu "
"$\\sigma_k.$ Stavy tohoto druhu se nazývají *separabilní stavy*. Tento "
"koncept lze rozšířit i na více než dva systémy.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Bullet: '4. '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"*Entangled states*. Not all states of pairs of systems are separable. In the"
" general formulation of quantum information, this is how entanglement is "
"defined: states that are not separable are said to be *entangled*.\n"
msgstr ""
"*Provázané stavy*. Ne všechny stavy dvojic systémů jsou separabilní. V "
"obecné formulaci kvantové informace se takto definuje provázanost "
"(entanglement): stavy, které nejsou separabilní, se nazývají *provázané*.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"   Note that this terminology is consistent with the terminology we used in "
"the \"Basics of quantum information\" course. There we said that quantum "
"state vectors that are not product states represent entangled states — and "
"indeed, for any quantum state vector $\\vert\\psi\\rangle$ that is not a "
"product state, we find that the state represented by the density matrix "
"$\\vert\\psi\\rangle\\langle\\psi\\vert$ is not separable. Entanglement is "
"much more complicated than this for states that are not pure.\n"
msgstr ""
"   Všimni si, že tato terminologie je konzistentní s terminologií, kterou "
"jsme používali v kurzu „Základy kvantové informace\". Tam jsme řekli, že "
"kvantové stavové vektory, které nejsou produktovými stavy, reprezentují "
"provázané stavy — a skutečně, pro jakýkoli kvantový stavový vektor "
"$\\vert\\psi\\rangle,$ který není produktovým stavem, zjistíme, že stav "
"reprezentovaný maticí hustoty $\\vert\\psi\\rangle\\langle\\psi\\vert$ není "
"separabilní. Provázanost je pro stavy, které nejsou čisté, mnohem "
"komplikovanější.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Title ##
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Reduced states and the partial trace {#reduced-states-and-the-partial-trace}"
msgstr ""
"Redukované stavy a parciální stopa {#reduced-states-and-the-partial-trace}"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"There's a simple but important thing we can do with density matrices in the context of multiple systems, which is to describe the states we obtain by ignoring some of the systems.\n"
"When multiple systems are in a quantum state and we discard or choose to ignore one or more of the systems,\n"
"the state of the remaining systems is called the *reduced state* of those systems.\n"
"Density matrix descriptions of reduced states are easily obtained through a mapping, known as the *partial trace*, from the density matrix describing the state of the whole.\n"
msgstr ""
"S maticemi hustoty v kontextu více systémů můžeme udělat jednu jednoduchou, ale důležitou věc, a tou je popsat stavy, které získáme ignorováním některých systémů.\n"
"Když je více systémů v kvantovém stavu a jeden nebo více z nich zahodíme nebo se rozhodneme ignorovat,\n"
"stav zbývajících systémů se nazývá *redukovaný stav* těchto systémů.\n"
"Popis redukovaných stavů pomocí matic hustoty lze snadno získat prostřednictvím zobrazení, známého jako *parciální stopa*, z matice hustoty popisující stav celku.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Title ###
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Example: reduced states for an e-bit {#example-reduced-states-for-an-e-bit}"
msgstr ""
"Příklad: redukované stavy pro e-bit {#example-reduced-states-for-an-e-bit}"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Suppose that we have a pair of qubits $(\\mathsf{A},\\mathsf{B})$ that are "
"together in the state\n"
msgstr ""
"Předpokládejme, že máme dvojici Qubitů $(\\mathsf{A},\\mathsf{B}),$ které "
"jsou společně ve stavu\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\vert\\phi^+\\rangle = \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}} \\vert 00 \\rangle + \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}} \\vert 11 \\rangle.\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\vert\\phi^+\\rangle = \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}} \\vert 00 \\rangle + \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}} \\vert 11 \\rangle.\n"
"$$\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"We can imagine that Alice holds the qubit $\\mathsf{A}$ and Bob holds $\\mathsf{B},$ which is to say that together they share an e-bit.\n"
"We'd like to have a density matrix description of Alice's qubit $\\mathsf{A}$ in isolation, as if Bob decided to take his qubit and visit the stars, never to be seen again.\n"
msgstr ""
"Můžeme si představit, že Alice drží qubit $\\mathsf{A}$ a Bob drží $\\mathsf{B},$ tedy dohromady sdílejí e-bit.\n"
"Rádi bychom měli popis Alicina Qubitu $\\mathsf{A}$ v izolaci pomocí matice hustoty, jako by se Bob rozhodl vzít svůj qubit a vydat se ke hvězdám, aby už nikdy nebyl spatřen.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"First let's think about what would happen if Bob decided somewhere on his journey to measure his qubit with respect to a standard basis measurement.\n"
"If he did this, he would obtain the outcome $0$ with probability\n"
msgstr ""
"Nejprve se zamysleme nad tím, co by se stalo, kdyby se Bob někde na své cestě rozhodl změřit svůj qubit standardním bázovým měřením.\n"
"Pokud by to udělal, získal by výsledek $0$ s pravděpodobností\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\bigl\\| \\bigl( \\mathbb{I}_{\\mathsf{A}} \\otimes \\langle 0\\vert \\bigr) \\vert \\phi^+ \\rangle \\bigr\\|^2\n"
"= \\Bigl\\| \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}} \\vert 0 \\rangle \\Bigr\\|^2 = \\frac{1}{2},\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\bigl\\| \\bigl( \\mathbb{I}_{\\mathsf{A}} \\otimes \\langle 0\\vert \\bigr) \\vert \\phi^+ \\rangle \\bigr\\|^2\n"
"= \\Bigl\\| \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}} \\vert 0 \\rangle \\Bigr\\|^2 = \\frac{1}{2},\n"
"$$\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"in which case the state of Alice's qubit becomes $\\vert 0\\rangle;$ and he "
"would obtain the outcome $1$ with probability\n"
msgstr ""
"v takovém případě se stav Alicina Qubitu stane $\\vert 0\\rangle;$ a "
"výsledek $1$ by získal s pravděpodobností\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\bigl\\| \\bigl( \\mathbb{I}_{\\mathsf{A}} \\otimes \\langle 1\\vert \\bigr) \\vert \\phi^+ \\rangle \\bigr\\|^2\n"
"= \\Bigl\\| \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}} \\vert 1 \\rangle \\Bigr\\|^2 = \\frac{1}{2},\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\bigl\\| \\bigl( \\mathbb{I}_{\\mathsf{A}} \\otimes \\langle 1\\vert \\bigr) \\vert \\phi^+ \\rangle \\bigr\\|^2\n"
"= \\Bigl\\| \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{2}} \\vert 1 \\rangle \\Bigr\\|^2 = \\frac{1}{2},\n"
"$$\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "in which case the state of Alice's qubit becomes $\\vert 1\\rangle.$\n"
msgstr "v takovém případě se stav Alicina Qubitu stane $\\vert 1\\rangle.$\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"So, if we ignore Bob's measurement outcome and focus on Alice's qubit, we conclude that she obtains the state $\\vert 0\\rangle$ with probability $1/2$ and the state $\\vert 1\\rangle$ with probability $1/2.$\n"
"This leads us to describe the state of Alice's qubit in isolation by the density matrix\n"
msgstr ""
"Takže pokud ignorujeme Bobův výsledek měření a zaměříme se na Alicin qubit, dojdeme k závěru, že získá stav $\\vert 0\\rangle$ s pravděpodobností $1/2$ a stav $\\vert 1\\rangle$ s pravděpodobností $1/2.$\n"
"To nás vede k popisu stavu Alicina Qubitu v izolaci pomocí matice hustoty\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\frac{1}{2} \\vert 0\\rangle\\langle 0\\vert + \\frac{1}{2} \\vert 1\\rangle\\langle 1\\vert = \\frac{1}{2} \\mathbb{I}_{\\mathsf{A}}.\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\frac{1}{2} \\vert 0\\rangle\\langle 0\\vert + \\frac{1}{2} \\vert 1\\rangle\\langle 1\\vert = \\frac{1}{2} \\mathbb{I}_{\\mathsf{A}}.\n"
"$$\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"That is, Alice's qubit is in the completely mixed state.\n"
"To be clear, this description of the state of Alice's qubit doesn't include Bob's measurement outcome; we're ignoring Bob altogether.\n"
msgstr ""
"To znamená, že Alicin qubit je v úplně smíšeném stavu.\n"
"Pro upřesnění, tento popis stavu Alicina Qubitu v izolaci nezahrnuje Bobův výsledek měření; Boba zcela ignorujeme.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Now, it might seem like the density matrix description of Alice's qubit in isolation that we've just obtained relies on the assumption that Bob has measured his qubit, but this is not actually so.\n"
"What we've done is to use the possibility that Bob measures his qubit to argue that the completely mixed state arises as the state of Alice's qubit, based on what we've already learned.\n"
"Of course, nothing says that Bob must measure his qubit — but nothing says that he doesn't.\n"
"And if he's light years away, then nothing he does or doesn't do can possibly influence the state of Alice's qubit viewed it in isolation.\n"
"That is to say, the description we've obtained for the state of Alice's qubit is the only description consistent with the impossibility of faster-than-light communication.\n"
msgstr ""
"Nyní se může zdát, že popis matice hustoty Alicina Qubitu v izolaci, který jsme právě získali, závisí na předpokladu, že Bob změřil svůj qubit, ale ve skutečnosti tomu tak není.\n"
"To, co jsme udělali, je, že jsme využili možnost, že Bob změří svůj qubit, abychom na základě toho, co jsme se již naučili, argumentovali, že úplně smíšený stav vznikne jako stav Alicina Qubitu.\n"
"Samozřejmě nic neříká, že Bob musí svůj qubit změřit — ale nic neříká, že to neudělá.\n"
"A pokud je vzdálen na světelné roky, pak nic, co udělá nebo neudělá, nemůže nijak ovlivnit stav Alicina Qubitu při pohledu v izolaci.\n"
"Jinými slovy, popis, který jsme získali pro stav Alicina Qubitu, je jediný popis konzistentní s nemožností komunikace rychlejší než světlo.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"We can also consider the state of Bob's qubit $\\mathsf{B},$ which happens to be the completely mixed state as well.\n"
"Indeed, for all four Bell states we find that the reduced state of both Alice's qubit and Bob's qubit is the completely mixed state.\n"
msgstr ""
"Můžeme také uvažovat stav Bobova Qubitu $\\mathsf{B},$ který je rovněž úplně smíšeným stavem.\n"
"Skutečně, pro všechny čtyři Bellovy stavy zjistíme, že redukovaný stav jak Alicina Qubitu, tak Bobova Qubitu je úplně smíšený stav.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Title ###
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Reduced states for a general quantum state vector {#reduced-states-for-a-"
"general-quantum-state-vector}"
msgstr ""
"Redukované stavy pro obecný kvantový stavový vektor {#reduced-states-for-a-"
"general-quantum-state-vector}"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Now let's generalize the example just discussed to two arbitrary systems $\\mathsf{A}$ and $\\mathsf{B},$ not necessarily qubits in the state $\\vert \\phi^+\\rangle.$\n"
"We'll assume the classical state sets of $\\mathsf{A}$ and $\\mathsf{B}$ are $\\Sigma$ and $\\Gamma,$ respectively.\n"
"A density matrix $\\rho$ representing a state of the combined system $(\\mathsf{A},\\mathsf{B})$ therefore has row and column indices corresponding to the Cartesian product $\\Sigma\\times\\Gamma.$\n"
msgstr ""
"Nyní zobecníme právě probíraný příklad na dva libovolné systémy $\\mathsf{A}$ a $\\mathsf{B},$ nemusí to být nutně Qubity ve stavu $\\vert \\phi^+\\rangle.$\n"
"Budeme předpokládat, že množiny klasických stavů systémů $\\mathsf{A}$ a $\\mathsf{B}$ jsou $\\Sigma$ a $\\Gamma,$ v daném pořadí.\n"
"Matice hustoty $\\rho$ reprezentující stav kombinovaného systému $(\\mathsf{A},\\mathsf{B})$ má tedy řádkové a sloupcové indexy odpovídající kartézskému součinu $\\Sigma\\times\\Gamma.$\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Suppose that the state of $(\\mathsf{A},\\mathsf{B})$ is described by the quantum state vector $\\vert\\psi\\rangle,$ so the density matrix describing this state is $\\rho = \\vert\\psi\\rangle\\langle\\psi\\vert.$\n"
"We'll obtain a density matrix description of the state of $\\mathsf{A}$ in isolation, which is conventionally denoted $\\rho_{\\mathsf{A}}.$\n"
"(A superscript is also sometimes used rather than a subscript.)\n"
msgstr ""
"Předpokládejme, že stav $(\\mathsf{A},\\mathsf{B})$ je popsán kvantovým stavovým vektorem $\\vert\\psi\\rangle,$ takže matice hustoty popisující tento stav je $\\rho = \\vert\\psi\\rangle\\langle\\psi\\vert.$\n"
"Získáme popis matice hustoty stavu systému $\\mathsf{A}$ v izolaci, který se konvenčně značí $\\rho_{\\mathsf{A}}.$\n"
"(Místo dolního indexu se někdy používá i horní index.)\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "The state vector $\\vert\\psi\\rangle$ can be expressed in the form\n"
msgstr "Stavový vektor $\\vert\\psi\\rangle$ lze vyjádřit ve tvaru\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\vert\\psi\\rangle = \\sum_{b\\in\\Gamma} \\vert\\phi_b\\rangle \\otimes \\vert b\\rangle\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\vert\\psi\\rangle = \\sum_{b\\in\\Gamma} \\vert\\phi_b\\rangle \\otimes \\vert b\\rangle\n"
"$$\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"for a uniquely determined collection of vectors $\\{\\vert\\phi_b\\rangle : b\\in\\Gamma\\}.$\n"
"In particular, these vectors can be determined through a simple formula.\n"
msgstr ""
"pro jednoznačně určenou kolekci vektorů $\\{\\vert\\phi_b\\rangle : b\\in\\Gamma\\}.$\n"
"Tyto vektory lze zejména určit pomocí jednoduchého vzorce.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\vert\\phi_b\\rangle = \\bigl(\\mathbb{I}_{\\mathsf{A}} \\otimes \\langle b\\vert\\bigr)\\vert\\psi\\rangle\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\vert\\phi_b\\rangle = \\bigl(\\mathbb{I}_{\\mathsf{A}} \\otimes \\langle b\\vert\\bigr)\\vert\\psi\\rangle\n"
"$$\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Reasoning similarly to the previous example of an e-bit, if we were to "
"measure the system $\\mathsf{B}$ with a standard basis measurement, we would"
" obtain each outcome $b\\in\\Gamma$ with probability "
"$\\|\\vert\\phi_b\\rangle\\|^2,$ in which case the state of $\\mathsf{A}$ "
"becomes\n"
msgstr ""
"Podobným uvažováním jako v předchozím příkladu s e-bitem, kdybychom měřili "
"systém $\\mathsf{B}$ měřením ve standardní bázi, získali bychom každý "
"výsledek $b\\in\\Gamma$ s pravděpodobností $\\|\\vert\\phi_b\\rangle\\|^2,$ "
"přičemž stav systému $\\mathsf{A}$ by se stal\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\frac{\\vert \\phi_b \\rangle}{\\|\\vert\\phi_b\\rangle\\|}.\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\frac{\\vert \\phi_b \\rangle}{\\|\\vert\\phi_b\\rangle\\|}.\n"
"$$\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "As a density matrix, this state can be written as follows.\n"
msgstr "Jako matici hustoty lze tento stav zapsat následovně.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\biggl(\\frac{\\vert \\phi_b \\rangle}{\\|\\vert\\phi_b\\rangle\\|}\\biggr)\n"
"\\biggl(\\frac{\\vert \\phi_b \\rangle}{\\|\\vert\\phi_b\\rangle\\|}\\biggr)^{\\dagger}\n"
"= \\frac{\\vert \\phi_b \\rangle\\langle\\phi_b\\vert}{\\|\\vert\\phi_b\\rangle\\|^2}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\biggl(\\frac{\\vert \\phi_b \\rangle}{\\|\\vert\\phi_b\\rangle\\|}\\biggr)\n"
"\\biggl(\\frac{\\vert \\phi_b \\rangle}{\\|\\vert\\phi_b\\rangle\\|}\\biggr)^{\\dagger}\n"
"= \\frac{\\vert \\phi_b \\rangle\\langle\\phi_b\\vert}{\\|\\vert\\phi_b\\rangle\\|^2}\n"
"$$\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Averaging the different states according to the probabilities of the "
"respective outcomes, we arrive at the density matrix\n"
msgstr ""
"Zprůměrováním různých stavů podle pravděpodobností příslušných výsledků "
"dospějeme k matici hustoty\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\rho_{\\mathsf{A}} = \\sum_{b\\in\\Gamma}\n"
"\\|\\vert\\phi_b\\rangle\\|^2 \\frac{\\vert \\phi_b \\rangle\\langle\\phi_b\\vert}{\\|\\vert\\phi_b\\rangle\\|^2}\n"
"= \\sum_{b\\in\\Gamma} \\vert \\phi_b \\rangle\\langle\\phi_b\\vert\n"
"= \\sum_{b\\in\\Gamma}\n"
"\\bigl(\\mathbb{I}_{\\mathsf{A}} \\otimes \\langle b\\vert\\bigr) \\vert\\psi\\rangle\\langle\\psi\\vert\n"
"\\bigl(\\mathbb{I}_{\\mathsf{A}} \\otimes \\vert b\\rangle\\bigr)\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\rho_{\\mathsf{A}} = \\sum_{b\\in\\Gamma}\n"
"\\|\\vert\\phi_b\\rangle\\|^2 \\frac{\\vert \\phi_b \\rangle\\langle\\phi_b\\vert}{\\|\\vert\\phi_b\\rangle\\|^2}\n"
"= \\sum_{b\\in\\Gamma} \\vert \\phi_b \\rangle\\langle\\phi_b\\vert\n"
"= \\sum_{b\\in\\Gamma}\n"
"\\bigl(\\mathbb{I}_{\\mathsf{A}} \\otimes \\langle b\\vert\\bigr) \\vert\\psi\\rangle\\langle\\psi\\vert\n"
"\\bigl(\\mathbb{I}_{\\mathsf{A}} \\otimes \\vert b\\rangle\\bigr)\n"
"$$\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Title ###
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "The partial trace {#the-partial-trace}"
msgstr "Parciální stopa {#the-partial-trace}"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "The formula\n"
msgstr "Vzorec\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\rho_{\\mathsf{A}}\n"
"= \\sum_{b\\in\\Gamma}\n"
"\\bigl(\\mathbb{I}_{\\mathsf{A}} \\otimes \\langle b\\vert\\bigr)\n"
"\\vert\\psi\\rangle\\langle\\psi\\vert\n"
"\\bigl(\\mathbb{I}_{\\mathsf{A}} \\otimes \\vert b\\rangle\\bigr)\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\rho_{\\mathsf{A}}\n"
"= \\sum_{b\\in\\Gamma}\n"
"\\bigl(\\mathbb{I}_{\\mathsf{A}} \\otimes \\langle b\\vert\\bigr)\n"
"\\vert\\psi\\rangle\\langle\\psi\\vert\n"
"\\bigl(\\mathbb{I}_{\\mathsf{A}} \\otimes \\vert b\\rangle\\bigr)\n"
"$$\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"leads us to the description of the reduced state of $\\mathsf{A}$ for any "
"density matrix $\\rho$ of the pair $(\\mathsf{A},\\mathsf{B}),$ not just a "
"pure state.\n"
msgstr ""
"nás vede k popisu redukovaného stavu systému $\\mathsf{A}$ pro libovolnou "
"matici hustoty $\\rho$ páru $(\\mathsf{A},\\mathsf{B}),$ nejen pro čistý "
"stav.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\rho_{\\mathsf{A}} = \\sum_{b\\in\\Gamma}\n"
"\\bigl( \\mathbb{I}_{\\mathsf{A}} \\otimes \\langle b \\vert\\bigr)\n"
"\\rho\n"
"\\bigl( \\mathbb{I}_{\\mathsf{A}} \\otimes \\vert b \\rangle\\bigr)\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\rho_{\\mathsf{A}} = \\sum_{b\\in\\Gamma}\n"
"\\bigl( \\mathbb{I}_{\\mathsf{A}} \\otimes \\langle b \\vert\\bigr)\n"
"\\rho\n"
"\\bigl( \\mathbb{I}_{\\mathsf{A}} \\otimes \\vert b \\rangle\\bigr)\n"
"$$\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"This formula must work, simply by linearity together with the fact that "
"every density matrix can be written as a convex combination of pure "
"states.\n"
msgstr ""
"Tento vzorec musí fungovat, jednoduše díky linearitě spolu s faktem, že "
"každou matici hustoty lze zapsat jako konvexní kombinaci čistých stavů.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The operation being performed on $\\rho$ to obtain $\\rho_{\\mathsf{A}}$ in this equation is known as the *partial trace*, and to be more precise we say that the partial trace is performed on $\\mathsf{B},$ or that $\\mathsf{B}$ is *traced out*.\n"
"This operation is denoted $\\operatorname{Tr}_{\\mathsf{B}},$ so we can write\n"
msgstr ""
"Operace prováděná na $\\rho$ k získání $\\rho_{\\mathsf{A}}$ v této rovnici je známá jako *parciální stopa*, a přesněji řečeno, parciální stopa se provádí přes $\\mathsf{B},$ neboli $\\mathsf{B}$ se *vystopuje*.\n"
"Tato operace se značí $\\operatorname{Tr}_{\\mathsf{B}},$ takže můžeme psát\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\operatorname{Tr}_{\\mathsf{B}} (\\rho) =\n"
"\\sum_{b\\in\\Gamma}\n"
"\\bigl( \\mathbb{I}_{\\mathsf{A}} \\otimes \\langle b \\vert\\bigr)\n"
"\\rho\n"
"\\bigl( \\mathbb{I}_{\\mathsf{A}} \\otimes \\vert b \\rangle\\bigr).\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\operatorname{Tr}_{\\mathsf{B}} (\\rho) =\n"
"\\sum_{b\\in\\Gamma}\n"
"\\bigl( \\mathbb{I}_{\\mathsf{A}} \\otimes \\langle b \\vert\\bigr)\n"
"\\rho\n"
"\\bigl( \\mathbb{I}_{\\mathsf{A}} \\otimes \\vert b \\rangle\\bigr).\n"
"$$\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"We can also define the partial trace on $\\mathsf{A},$ so it's the system "
"$\\mathsf{A}$ that gets traced out rather than $\\mathsf{B},$ like this.\n"
msgstr ""
"Můžeme také definovat parciální stopu přes $\\mathsf{A},$ takže je to systém"
" $\\mathsf{A},$ který se vystopuje místo $\\mathsf{B},$ takto.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\operatorname{Tr}_{\\mathsf{A}} (\\rho) =\n"
"\\sum_{a\\in\\Sigma}\n"
"\\bigl(\\langle a \\vert\\otimes\\mathbb{I}_{\\mathsf{B}}\\bigr)\n"
"\\rho\n"
"\\bigl(\\vert a \\rangle\\otimes\\mathbb{I}_{\\mathsf{B}}\\bigr)\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\operatorname{Tr}_{\\mathsf{A}} (\\rho) =\n"
"\\sum_{a\\in\\Sigma}\n"
"\\bigl(\\langle a \\vert\\otimes\\mathbb{I}_{\\mathsf{B}}\\bigr)\n"
"\\rho\n"
"\\bigl(\\vert a \\rangle\\otimes\\mathbb{I}_{\\mathsf{B}}\\bigr)\n"
"$$\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"This gives us the density matrix description $\\rho_{\\mathsf{B}}$ of the "
"state of $\\mathsf{B}$ in isolation rather than $\\mathsf{A}.$\n"
msgstr ""
"To nám dává popis matice hustoty $\\rho_{\\mathsf{B}}$ stavu systému "
"$\\mathsf{B}$ v izolaci místo systému $\\mathsf{A}.$\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"To recapitulate, if $(\\mathsf{A},\\mathsf{B})$ is any pair of systems and "
"we have a density matrix $\\rho$ describing a state of "
"$(\\mathsf{A},\\mathsf{B}),$ the *reduced states* of the systems "
"$\\mathsf{A}$ and $\\mathsf{B}$ are as follows.\n"
msgstr ""
"Abychom shrnuli, pokud $(\\mathsf{A},\\mathsf{B})$ je libovolný pár systémů "
"a máme matici hustoty $\\rho$ popisující stav $(\\mathsf{A},\\mathsf{B}),$ "
"*redukované stavy* systémů $\\mathsf{A}$ a $\\mathsf{B}$ jsou následující.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{aligned}\n"
"\\rho_{\\mathsf{A}} & = \\operatorname{Tr}_{\\mathsf{B}}(\\rho)\n"
"= \\sum_{b\\in\\Gamma} \\bigl( \\mathbb{I}_{\\mathsf{A}} \\otimes \\langle b \\vert\\bigr) \\rho \\bigl( \\mathbb{I}_{\\mathsf{A}} \\otimes \\vert b \\rangle\\bigr)\\\\[2mm]\n"
"\\rho_{\\mathsf{B}} & = \\operatorname{Tr}_{\\mathsf{A}}(\\rho) = \\sum_{a\\in\\Sigma}\n"
"\\bigl( \\langle a \\vert \\otimes \\mathbb{I}_{\\mathsf{B}}\\bigr) \\rho\n"
"\\bigl( \\vert a \\rangle\\otimes \\mathbb{I}_{\\mathsf{B}} \\bigr)\n"
"\\end{aligned}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{aligned}\n"
"\\rho_{\\mathsf{A}} & = \\operatorname{Tr}_{\\mathsf{B}}(\\rho)\n"
"= \\sum_{b\\in\\Gamma} \\bigl( \\mathbb{I}_{\\mathsf{A}} \\otimes \\langle b \\vert\\bigr) \\rho \\bigl( \\mathbb{I}_{\\mathsf{A}} \\otimes \\vert b \\rangle\\bigr)\\\\[2mm]\n"
"\\rho_{\\mathsf{B}} & = \\operatorname{Tr}_{\\mathsf{A}}(\\rho) = \\sum_{a\\in\\Sigma}\n"
"\\bigl( \\langle a \\vert \\otimes \\mathbb{I}_{\\mathsf{B}}\\bigr) \\rho\n"
"\\bigl( \\vert a \\rangle\\otimes \\mathbb{I}_{\\mathsf{B}} \\bigr)\n"
"\\end{aligned}\n"
"$$\n"
"Pokud $\\rho$ je matice hustoty, pak $\\rho_{\\mathsf{A}}$ a $\\rho_{\\mathsf{B}}$ budou také nutně matice hustoty.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"If $\\rho$ is a density matrix, then $\\rho_{\\mathsf{A}}$ and "
"$\\rho_{\\mathsf{B}}$ will also necessarily be density matrices.\n"
msgstr ""
"Tyto pojmy lze přirozeným způsobem zobecnit na libovolný počet systémů místo dvou.\n"
"Obecně můžeme do dolního indexu matice hustoty $\\rho$ vložit názvy libovolných systémů, které si zvolíme, a popsat tak redukovaný stav právě těchto systémů.\n"
"Například pokud $\\mathsf{A},$ $\\mathsf{B}$ a $\\mathsf{C}$ jsou systémy a $\\rho$ je matice hustoty popisující stav $(\\mathsf{A},\\mathsf{B},\\mathsf{C}),$ pak můžeme definovat\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"These notions can be generalized to any number of systems in place of two in a natural way.\n"
"In general, we can put the names of whatever systems we choose in the subscript of a density matrix $\\rho$ to describe the reduced state of just those systems.\n"
"For example, if $\\mathsf{A},$ $\\mathsf{B},$ and $\\mathsf{C}$ are systems and $\\rho$ is a density matrix describing a state of $(\\mathsf{A},\\mathsf{B},\\mathsf{C}),$ then we can define\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{aligned}\n"
"\\rho_{\\mathsf{AC}} & = \\operatorname{Tr}_{\\mathsf{B}}(\\rho) = \\sum_{b\\in\\Gamma}\n"
"\\bigl( \\mathbb{I}_{\\mathsf{A}} \\otimes \\langle b \\vert \\otimes \\mathbb{I}_{\\mathsf{C}} \\bigr) \\rho\n"
"\\bigl( \\mathbb{I}_{\\mathsf{A}} \\otimes \\vert b \\rangle \\otimes \\mathbb{I}_{\\mathsf{C}} \\bigr) \\\\[2mm]\n"
"\\rho_{\\mathsf{C}} & = \\operatorname{Tr}_{\\mathsf{AB}}(\\rho) = \\sum_{a\\in\\Sigma} \\sum_{b\\in\\Gamma}\n"
"\\bigl( \\langle a \\vert \\otimes \\langle b \\vert \\otimes \\mathbb{I}_{\\mathsf{C}} \\bigr) \\rho\n"
"\\bigl( \\vert a \\rangle \\otimes \\vert b \\rangle \\otimes \\mathbb{I}_{\\mathsf{C}} \\bigr)\n"
"\\end{aligned}\n"
"$$\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{aligned}\n"
"\\rho_{\\mathsf{AC}} & = \\operatorname{Tr}_{\\mathsf{B}}(\\rho) = \\sum_{b\\in\\Gamma}\n"
"\\bigl( \\mathbb{I}_{\\mathsf{A}} \\otimes \\langle b \\vert \\otimes \\mathbb{I}_{\\mathsf{C}} \\bigr) \\rho\n"
"\\bigl( \\mathbb{I}_{\\mathsf{A}} \\otimes \\vert b \\rangle \\otimes \\mathbb{I}_{\\mathsf{C}} \\bigr) \\\\[2mm]\n"
"\\rho_{\\mathsf{C}} & = \\operatorname{Tr}_{\\mathsf{AB}}(\\rho) = \\sum_{a\\in\\Sigma} \\sum_{b\\in\\Gamma}\n"
"\\bigl( \\langle a \\vert \\otimes \\langle b \\vert \\otimes \\mathbb{I}_{\\mathsf{C}} \\bigr) \\rho\n"
"\\bigl( \\vert a \\rangle \\otimes \\vert b \\rangle \\otimes \\mathbb{I}_{\\mathsf{C}} \\bigr)\n"
"\\end{aligned}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr "a analogicky pro další volby systémů.\n"

#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "and similarly for other choices for the systems.\n"
msgstr ""

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Title ###
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Alternative description of the partial trace {#alternative-description-of-"
"the-partial-trace}"
msgstr ""
"Alternativní popis parciální stopy {#alternative-description-of-the-partial-"
"trace}"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"An alternative way to describe the partial trace mappings "
"$\\operatorname{Tr}_{\\mathsf{A}}$ and $\\operatorname{Tr}_{\\mathsf{B}}$ is"
" that they are the *unique* linear mappings that satisfy the formulas\n"
msgstr ""
"Alternativní způsob, jak popsat zobrazení parciální stopy "
"$\\operatorname{Tr}_{\\mathsf{A}}$ a $\\operatorname{Tr}_{\\mathsf{B}},$ je,"
" že jsou to *jedinečná* lineární zobrazení splňující vzorce\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{aligned}\n"
"\\operatorname{Tr}_{\\mathsf{A}}(M \\otimes N) & = \\operatorname{Tr}(M) N \\\\[2mm]\n"
"\\operatorname{Tr}_{\\mathsf{B}}(M \\otimes N) & = \\operatorname{Tr}(N) M.\n"
"\\end{aligned}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{aligned}\n"
"\\operatorname{Tr}_{\\mathsf{A}}(M \\otimes N) & = \\operatorname{Tr}(M) N \\\\[2mm]\n"
"\\operatorname{Tr}_{\\mathsf{B}}(M \\otimes N) & = \\operatorname{Tr}(N) M.\n"
"\\end{aligned}\n"
"$$\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"In these formulas, $N$ and $M$ are square matrices of the appropriate sizes:\n"
"the rows and columns of $M$ correspond to the classical states of $\\mathsf{A}$ and the rows and columns of $N$ correspond to the classical states of $\\mathsf{B}.$\n"
msgstr ""
"V těchto vzorcích jsou $N$ a $M$ čtvercové matice příslušných rozměrů:\n"
"řádky a sloupce $M$ odpovídají klasickým stavům systému $\\mathsf{A}$ a řádky a sloupce $N$ odpovídají klasickým stavům systému $\\mathsf{B}.$\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"This characterization of the partial trace is not only fundamental from a mathematical viewpoint, but can also allow for quick calculations in some situations.\n"
"For example, consider this state of a pair of qubits $(\\mathsf{A},\\mathsf{B}).$\n"
msgstr ""
"Tato charakterizace parciální stopy je nejen fundamentální z matematického hlediska, ale v některých situacích také umožňuje rychlé výpočty.\n"
"Uvažuj například tento stav páru Qubitů $(\\mathsf{A},\\mathsf{B}).$\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\rho =\n"
"\\frac{1}{2} \\vert 0\\rangle\\langle 0\\vert \\otimes \\vert 0\\rangle\\langle 0\\vert +\n"
"\\frac{1}{2} \\vert 1\\rangle\\langle 1\\vert \\otimes \\vert +\\rangle\\langle +\\vert\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\rho =\n"
"\\frac{1}{2} \\vert 0\\rangle\\langle 0\\vert \\otimes \\vert 0\\rangle\\langle 0\\vert +\n"
"\\frac{1}{2} \\vert 1\\rangle\\langle 1\\vert \\otimes \\vert +\\rangle\\langle +\\vert\n"
"$$\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"To compute the reduced state $\\rho_{\\mathsf{A}}$ for instance, we can use linearity together with the fact that\n"
"$\\vert 0\\rangle\\langle 0\\vert$ and $\\vert +\\rangle\\langle +\\vert$ have unit trace.\n"
msgstr ""
"Pro výpočet redukovaného stavu $\\rho_{\\mathsf{A}}$ například můžeme využít linearitu spolu s faktem, že\n"
"$\\vert 0\\rangle\\langle 0\\vert$ a $\\vert +\\rangle\\langle +\\vert$ mají jednotkovou stopu.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\rho_{\\mathsf{A}} =\n"
"\\operatorname{Tr}_{\\mathsf{B}}(\\rho) =\n"
"\\frac{1}{2} \\operatorname{Tr}\\bigl(\\vert 0\\rangle\\langle 0\\vert\\bigr)\\, \\vert 0\\rangle\\langle 0\\vert  +\n"
"\\frac{1}{2} \\operatorname{Tr}\\bigl(\\vert +\\rangle\\langle +\\vert\\bigr) \\vert 1\\rangle\\langle 1\\vert =\n"
"\\frac{1}{2} \\vert 0\\rangle\\langle 0\\vert + \\frac{1}{2} \\vert 1\\rangle\\langle 1\\vert\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\rho_{\\mathsf{A}} =\n"
"\\operatorname{Tr}_{\\mathsf{B}}(\\rho) =\n"
"\\frac{1}{2} \\operatorname{Tr}\\bigl(\\vert 0\\rangle\\langle 0\\vert\\bigr)\\, \\vert 0\\rangle\\langle 0\\vert  +\n"
"\\frac{1}{2} \\operatorname{Tr}\\bigl(\\vert +\\rangle\\langle +\\vert\\bigr) \\vert 1\\rangle\\langle 1\\vert =\n"
"\\frac{1}{2} \\vert 0\\rangle\\langle 0\\vert + \\frac{1}{2} \\vert 1\\rangle\\langle 1\\vert\n"
"$$\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "The reduced state $\\rho_{\\mathsf{B}}$ can be computed similarly.\n"
msgstr "Redukovaný stav $\\rho_{\\mathsf{B}}$ lze vypočítat podobně.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\rho_{\\mathsf{B}} =\n"
"\\operatorname{Tr}_{\\mathsf{A}}(\\rho) =\n"
"\\frac{1}{2} \\operatorname{Tr}\\bigl(\\vert 0\\rangle\\langle 0\\vert\\bigr)\\, \\vert 0\\rangle\\langle 0\\vert  +\n"
"\\frac{1}{2} \\operatorname{Tr}\\bigl(\\vert 1\\rangle\\langle 1\\vert\\bigr) \\vert +\\rangle\\langle +\\vert =\n"
"\\frac{1}{2} \\vert 0\\rangle\\langle 0\\vert + \\frac{1}{2} \\vert +\\rangle\\langle +\\vert\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\rho_{\\mathsf{B}} =\n"
"\\operatorname{Tr}_{\\mathsf{A}}(\\rho) =\n"
"\\frac{1}{2} \\operatorname{Tr}\\bigl(\\vert 0\\rangle\\langle 0\\vert\\bigr)\\, \\vert 0\\rangle\\langle 0\\vert  +\n"
"\\frac{1}{2} \\operatorname{Tr}\\bigl(\\vert 1\\rangle\\langle 1\\vert\\bigr) \\vert +\\rangle\\langle +\\vert =\n"
"\\frac{1}{2} \\vert 0\\rangle\\langle 0\\vert + \\frac{1}{2} \\vert +\\rangle\\langle +\\vert\n"
"$$\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Title ###
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "The partial trace for two qubits {#the-partial-trace-for-two-qubits}"
msgstr "Parciální stopa pro dva Qubity {#the-partial-trace-for-two-qubits}"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The partial trace can also be described explicitly in terms of matrices.\n"
"Here we'll do this just for two qubits, but this can also be generalized to larger systems.\n"
"Assume that we have two qubits $(\\mathsf{A},\\mathsf{B}),$ so that any density matrix describing a state of these two qubits can be written as\n"
msgstr ""
"Parciální stopu lze také popsat explicitně pomocí matic.\n"
"Zde to provedeme jen pro dva Qubity, ale lze to zobecnit i na větší systémy.\n"
"Předpokládejme, že máme dva Qubity $(\\mathsf{A},\\mathsf{B}),$ takže libovolnou matici hustoty popisující stav těchto dvou Qubitů lze zapsat jako\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\rho = \\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"\\alpha_{00} & \\alpha_{01} & \\alpha_{02} & \\alpha_{03}\\\\[2mm]\n"
"\\alpha_{10} & \\alpha_{11} & \\alpha_{12} & \\alpha_{13}\\\\[2mm]\n"
"\\alpha_{20} & \\alpha_{21} & \\alpha_{22} & \\alpha_{23}\\\\[2mm]\n"
"\\alpha_{30} & \\alpha_{31} & \\alpha_{32} & \\alpha_{33}\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\rho = \\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"\\alpha_{00} & \\alpha_{01} & \\alpha_{02} & \\alpha_{03}\\\\[2mm]\n"
"\\alpha_{10} & \\alpha_{11} & \\alpha_{12} & \\alpha_{13}\\\\[2mm]\n"
"\\alpha_{20} & \\alpha_{21} & \\alpha_{22} & \\alpha_{23}\\\\[2mm]\n"
"\\alpha_{30} & \\alpha_{31} & \\alpha_{32} & \\alpha_{33}\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\n"
"$$\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "for some choice of complex numbers $\\{\\alpha_{jk} : 0\\leq j,k\\leq 3\\}.$\n"
msgstr "pro nějakou volbu komplexních čísel $\\{\\alpha_{jk} : 0\\leq j,k\\leq 3\\}.$\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "The partial trace over the first system has the following formula.\n"
msgstr "Parciální stopa přes první systém má následující vzorec.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\operatorname{Tr}_{\\mathsf{A}} \\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"\\alpha_{00} & \\alpha_{01} & \\alpha_{02} & \\alpha_{03}\\\\[2mm]\n"
"\\alpha_{10} & \\alpha_{11} & \\alpha_{12} & \\alpha_{13}\\\\[2mm]\n"
"\\alpha_{20} & \\alpha_{21} & \\alpha_{22} & \\alpha_{23}\\\\[2mm]\n"
"\\alpha_{30} & \\alpha_{31} & \\alpha_{32} & \\alpha_{33}\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\n"
"= \\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"\\alpha_{00} & \\alpha_{01} \\\\[2mm]\n"
"\\alpha_{10} & \\alpha_{11}\n"
"\\end{pmatrix} +\n"
"\\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"\\alpha_{22} & \\alpha_{23}\\\\[2mm]\n"
"\\alpha_{32} & \\alpha_{33}\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\n"
"= \\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"\\alpha_{00} + \\alpha_{22} & \\alpha_{01} + \\alpha_{23}\\\\[2mm]\n"
"\\alpha_{10} + \\alpha_{32} & \\alpha_{11} + \\alpha_{33}\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\operatorname{Tr}_{\\mathsf{A}} \\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"\\alpha_{00} & \\alpha_{01} & \\alpha_{02} & \\alpha_{03}\\\\[2mm]\n"
"\\alpha_{10} & \\alpha_{11} & \\alpha_{12} & \\alpha_{13}\\\\[2mm]\n"
"\\alpha_{20} & \\alpha_{21} & \\alpha_{22} & \\alpha_{23}\\\\[2mm]\n"
"\\alpha_{30} & \\alpha_{31} & \\alpha_{32} & \\alpha_{33}\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\n"
"= \\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"\\alpha_{00} & \\alpha_{01} \\\\[2mm]\n"
"\\alpha_{10} & \\alpha_{11}\n"
"\\end{pmatrix} +\n"
"\\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"\\alpha_{22} & \\alpha_{23}\\\\[2mm]\n"
"\\alpha_{32} & \\alpha_{33}\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\n"
"= \\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"\\alpha_{00} + \\alpha_{22} & \\alpha_{01} + \\alpha_{23}\\\\[2mm]\n"
"\\alpha_{10} + \\alpha_{32} & \\alpha_{11} + \\alpha_{33}\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\n"
"$$\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"One way to think about this formula begins by viewing $4\\times 4$ matrices as $2\\times 2$ block matrices, where each block is $2\\times 2.$\n"
"That is,\n"
"$$\n"
"\\rho = \\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"M_{0,0} & M_{0,1} \\\\[1mm]\n"
"M_{1,0} & M_{1,1}\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"Jeden způsob, jak o tomto vzorci přemýšlet, začíná pohledem na $4\\times 4$ matice jako na $2\\times 2$ blokové matice, kde každý blok je $2\\times 2.$\n"
"To znamená,\n"
"$$\n"
"\\rho = \\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"M_{0,0} & M_{0,1} \\\\[1mm]\n"
"M_{1,0} & M_{1,1}\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\n"
"$$\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "for\n"
msgstr "pro\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"M_{0,0} = \\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"\\alpha_{00} & \\alpha_{01} \\\\[2mm]\n"
"\\alpha_{10} & \\alpha_{11}\n"
"\\end{pmatrix},\n"
"\\quad\n"
"M_{0,1} = \\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"\\alpha_{02} & \\alpha_{03} \\\\[2mm]\n"
"\\alpha_{12} & \\alpha_{13}\n"
"\\end{pmatrix},\n"
"\\quad\n"
"M_{1,0} = \\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"\\alpha_{20} & \\alpha_{21} \\\\[2mm]\n"
"\\alpha_{30} & \\alpha_{31}\n"
"\\end{pmatrix},\n"
"\\quad\n"
"M_{1,1} = \\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"\\alpha_{22} & \\alpha_{23} \\\\[2mm]\n"
"\\alpha_{32} & \\alpha_{33}\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}.\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"M_{0,0} = \\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"\\alpha_{00} & \\alpha_{01} \\\\[2mm]\n"
"\\alpha_{10} & \\alpha_{11}\n"
"\\end{pmatrix},\n"
"\\quad\n"
"M_{0,1} = \\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"\\alpha_{02} & \\alpha_{03} \\\\[2mm]\n"
"\\alpha_{12} & \\alpha_{13}\n"
"\\end{pmatrix},\n"
"\\quad\n"
"M_{1,0} = \\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"\\alpha_{20} & \\alpha_{21} \\\\[2mm]\n"
"\\alpha_{30} & \\alpha_{31}\n"
"\\end{pmatrix},\n"
"\\quad\n"
"M_{1,1} = \\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"\\alpha_{22} & \\alpha_{23} \\\\[2mm]\n"
"\\alpha_{32} & \\alpha_{33}\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}.\n"
"$$\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "We then have\n"
msgstr "Pak máme\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\operatorname{Tr}_{\\mathsf{A}}\\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"M_{0,0} & M_{0,1} \\\\[1mm]\n"
"M_{1,0} & M_{1,1}\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\n"
"= M_{0,0} + M_{1,1}.\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\operatorname{Tr}_{\\mathsf{A}}\\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"M_{0,0} & M_{0,1} \\\\[1mm]\n"
"M_{1,0} & M_{1,1}\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\n"
"= M_{0,0} + M_{1,1}.\n"
"$$\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Here's the formula when the second system is traced out rather than the "
"first.\n"
msgstr ""
"Zde je vzorec pro případ, kdy se trasuje přes druhý systém místo prvního.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\operatorname{Tr}_{\\mathsf{B}}\n"
"\\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"\\alpha_{00} & \\alpha_{01} & \\alpha_{02} & \\alpha_{03}\\\\[2mm]\n"
"\\alpha_{10} & \\alpha_{11} & \\alpha_{12} & \\alpha_{13}\\\\[2mm]\n"
"\\alpha_{20} & \\alpha_{21} & \\alpha_{22} & \\alpha_{23}\\\\[2mm]\n"
"\\alpha_{30} & \\alpha_{31} & \\alpha_{32} & \\alpha_{33}\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\n"
"= \\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"\\operatorname{Tr} \\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"\\alpha_{00} & \\alpha_{01}\\\\[1mm]\n"
"\\alpha_{10} & \\alpha_{11}\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\n"
"&\n"
"\\operatorname{Tr} \\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"\\alpha_{02} & \\alpha_{03}\\\\[1mm]\n"
"\\alpha_{12} & \\alpha_{13}\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\n"
"\\\\[4mm]\n"
"\\operatorname{Tr} \\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"\\alpha_{20} & \\alpha_{21}\\\\[1mm]\n"
"\\alpha_{30} & \\alpha_{31}\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\n"
"&\n"
"\\operatorname{Tr} \\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"\\alpha_{22} & \\alpha_{23}\\\\[1mm]\n"
"\\alpha_{32} & \\alpha_{33}\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\n"
"= \\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"\\alpha_{00} + \\alpha_{11} & \\alpha_{02} + \\alpha_{13}\\\\[2mm]\n"
"\\alpha_{20} + \\alpha_{31} & \\alpha_{22} + \\alpha_{33}\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\operatorname{Tr}_{\\mathsf{B}}\n"
"\\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"\\alpha_{00} & \\alpha_{01} & \\alpha_{02} & \\alpha_{03}\\\\[2mm]\n"
"\\alpha_{10} & \\alpha_{11} & \\alpha_{12} & \\alpha_{13}\\\\[2mm]\n"
"\\alpha_{20} & \\alpha_{21} & \\alpha_{22} & \\alpha_{23}\\\\[2mm]\n"
"\\alpha_{30} & \\alpha_{31} & \\alpha_{32} & \\alpha_{33}\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\n"
"= \\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"\\operatorname{Tr} \\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"\\alpha_{00} & \\alpha_{01}\\\\[1mm]\n"
"\\alpha_{10} & \\alpha_{11}\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\n"
"&\n"
"\\operatorname{Tr} \\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"\\alpha_{02} & \\alpha_{03}\\\\[1mm]\n"
"\\alpha_{12} & \\alpha_{13}\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\n"
"\\\\[4mm]\n"
"\\operatorname{Tr} \\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"\\alpha_{20} & \\alpha_{21}\\\\[1mm]\n"
"\\alpha_{30} & \\alpha_{31}\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\n"
"&\n"
"\\operatorname{Tr} \\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"\\alpha_{22} & \\alpha_{23}\\\\[1mm]\n"
"\\alpha_{32} & \\alpha_{33}\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\n"
"= \\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"\\alpha_{00} + \\alpha_{11} & \\alpha_{02} + \\alpha_{13}\\\\[2mm]\n"
"\\alpha_{20} + \\alpha_{31} & \\alpha_{22} + \\alpha_{33}\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\n"
"$$\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"In terms of block matrices of a form similar to before, we have this "
"formula.\n"
msgstr ""
"Pomocí blokových matic ve tvaru podobném předchozímu máme tento vzorec.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\operatorname{Tr}_{\\mathsf{B}}\n"
"\\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"M_{0,0} & M_{0,1} \\\\[1mm]\n"
"M_{1,0} & M_{1,1}\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\n"
"= \\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"\\operatorname{Tr}(M_{0,0}) & \\operatorname{Tr}(M_{0,1}) \\\\[1mm]\n"
"\\operatorname{Tr}(M_{1,0}) & \\operatorname{Tr}(M_{1,1})\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\operatorname{Tr}_{\\mathsf{B}}\n"
"\\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"M_{0,0} & M_{0,1} \\\\[1mm]\n"
"M_{1,0} & M_{1,1}\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\n"
"= \\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"\\operatorname{Tr}(M_{0,0}) & \\operatorname{Tr}(M_{0,1}) \\\\[1mm]\n"
"\\operatorname{Tr}(M_{1,0}) & \\operatorname{Tr}(M_{1,1})\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\n"
"$$\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The block matrix descriptions of these functions can be extended to systems "
"larger than qubits in a natural and direct way.\n"
msgstr ""
"Popis těchto funkcí pomocí blokových matic lze přirozeným a přímým způsobem "
"rozšířit na systémy větší než qubit​y.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"To finish the lesson, let's apply these formulas to the same state we "
"considered above.\n"
msgstr ""
"Na závěr lekce aplikujme tyto vzorce na tentýž stav, který jsme uvažovali "
"výše.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\rho = \\frac{1}{2} \\vert 0\\rangle \\langle 0 \\vert \\otimes \\vert 0\\rangle \\langle 0 \\vert\n"
"+ \\frac{1}{2} \\vert 1\\rangle \\langle 1 \\vert \\otimes \\vert +\\rangle \\langle + \\vert\n"
"=\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\rho = \\frac{1}{2} \\vert 0\\rangle \\langle 0 \\vert \\otimes \\vert 0\\rangle \\langle 0 \\vert\n"
"+ \\frac{1}{2} \\vert 1\\rangle \\langle 1 \\vert \\otimes \\vert +\\rangle \\langle + \\vert\n"
"=\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"\\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"\\frac{1}{2} & 0 & 0 & 0\\\\[2mm]\n"
"0 & 0 & 0 & 0 \\\\[2mm]\n"
"0 & 0 & \\frac{1}{4} & \\frac{1}{4}\\\\[2mm]\n"
"0 & 0 & \\frac{1}{4} & \\frac{1}{4}\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}.\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"\\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"\\frac{1}{2} & 0 & 0 & 0\\\\[2mm]\n"
"0 & 0 & 0 & 0 \\\\[2mm]\n"
"0 & 0 & \\frac{1}{4} & \\frac{1}{4}\\\\[2mm]\n"
"0 & 0 & \\frac{1}{4} & \\frac{1}{4}\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}.\n"
"$$\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "The reduced state of the first system $\\mathsf{A}$ is\n"
msgstr "Redukovaný stav prvního systému $\\mathsf{A}$ je\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\operatorname{Tr}_{\\mathsf{B}}\n"
"\\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"\\frac{1}{2} & 0 & 0 & 0\\\\[2mm]\n"
"0 & 0 & 0 & 0\\\\[2mm]\n"
"0 & 0 & \\frac{1}{4} & \\frac{1}{4}\\\\[2mm]\n"
"0 & 0 & \\frac{1}{4} & \\frac{1}{4}\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\n"
"= \\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"\\operatorname{Tr} \\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"\\frac{1}{2} & 0\\\\[1mm]\n"
"0 & 0\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\n"
"&\n"
"\\operatorname{Tr} \\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"0 & 0\\\\[1mm]\n"
"0 & 0\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\n"
"\\\\[4mm]\n"
"\\operatorname{Tr} \\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"0 & 0\\\\[1mm]\n"
"0 & 0\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\n"
"&\n"
"\\operatorname{Tr} \\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"\\frac{1}{4} & \\frac{1}{4}\\\\[2mm]\n"
"\\frac{1}{4} & \\frac{1}{4}\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\n"
"= \\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"\\frac{1}{2} & 0\\\\[2mm]\n"
"0 & \\frac{1}{2}\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\operatorname{Tr}_{\\mathsf{B}}\n"
"\\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"\\frac{1}{2} & 0 & 0 & 0\\\\[2mm]\n"
"0 & 0 & 0 & 0\\\\[2mm]\n"
"0 & 0 & \\frac{1}{4} & \\frac{1}{4}\\\\[2mm]\n"
"0 & 0 & \\frac{1}{4} & \\frac{1}{4}\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\n"
"= \\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"\\operatorname{Tr} \\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"\\frac{1}{2} & 0\\\\[1mm]\n"
"0 & 0\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\n"
"&\n"
